{"clock":1,"nonce":"6a9afa1bc4bd6a79fe0d869c9f90b661","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1791552891,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/EPFL-ENAC/eesd-modern-masonry-walls-db","event":"issue:5778983108"},"data":{"body":"**TL;DR**\n- **What:** re-pin `epfl-design-system` in `frontend/package.json` from `#30818ba…` to `#55fc0a8b7fcff0bf5533923a88ed66ab41023c8d` (current `main` of EPFL-ENAC/epfl-design-skill), reinstall, rebuild, deploy.\n- **Why:** the pinned commit is gone from epfl-design-skill's history and will stop resolving, which breaks `pnpm install`. It also bundles Suisse Int'l's **desktop** font files, which the app serves as web fonts; EPFL's licence only allows the delivered webfont files on the web.\n- **User impact:** same font, now loaded from `https://enac-it-fonts.epfl.ch`. Text set in Light (300) renders in Regular until a Light webfont exists.\n- **Effort:** small\n\n---\n\n## What happens now\n\n`frontend/src/css/epfl.css` imports `epfl-design-system/css/epfl.css`. At `30818ba`, its token layer declares `@font-face` rules pointing at `fonts/SuisseIntl-*.ttf`, the seven desktop TTFs. Vite copies them into `dist/spa/assets/`, so prod (`modernmasonrydatabase.epfl.ch`) and dev (`modernmasonrydb-dev.epfl.ch`) both serve them (checked 2026-10-09), and every image built from this repo contains them.\n\nOn 2026-10-09, epfl-design-skill removed the font files from its whole history (EPFL-ENAC/epfl-design-skill#3): every commit hash changed, and `30818ba` is no longer on any branch. It still resolves only until GitHub garbage-collects it; after that, `pnpm install` fails.\n\n## What we propose\n\nPin the current `main`, `55fc0a8b7fcff0bf5533923a88ed66ab41023c8d`. Between the old pin and it, the only changes under `css/`, `kits/`, `tokens/` and `assets/` are the font:\n\n- `tokens/colors_and_type.css` now `@import`s `tokens/fonts.css`, six woff2 faces served by `https://enac-it-fonts.epfl.ch`: 400, 400 italic, 500, 600, 600 italic, 700.\n- The server answers `*.epfl.ch` origins, so prod and dev work as they are. Local dev (`http://localhost:\u003cport\u003e`) gets the font from the EPFL network or VPN; elsewhere text falls back to Arial.\n\nDo not pin `b31cefe…`, the rewritten twin of `30818ba`: it has no font files left, so its `@font-face` rules point at nothing.\n\n## Visible change\n\nThere is no Light (300) or Medium italic webfont yet; the browser uses the nearest face. This app sets `font-weight: var(--w-light)` in `DonutFigure.vue`, `DocumentationPage.vue`, `OthersPage.vue`, `OverviewPage.vue`, `SubmitPage.vue`, and `EpflKeyNumber` does too: that text will look slightly heavier.\n\n## Done when\n\n- [ ] `frontend/package.json` and `pnpm-lock.yaml` point at `55fc0a8b7fcff0bf5533923a88ed66ab41023c8d`\n- [ ] `pnpm build`: no `.ttf` in `dist/`\n- [ ] Prod and dev redeployed; the old `/assets/SuisseIntl-*.ttf` URLs return 404; the Network tab shows the `.woff2` files from `enac-it-fonts.epfl.ch` with status 200\n- [ ] Older images that contain the TTFs: check the package's visibility and delete those versions if anyone outside EPFL can pull them\n","title":"[BUG](Frontend) Re-pin the design system: pinned commit is gone and ships desktop font files"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1792766763,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/EPFL-ENAC/eesd-modern-masonry-walls-db","event":"issue:5778983108"},"data":{"add":["bug","assignee:sphamba"],"remove":null}},{"kind":"comment","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1792766760,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/EPFL-ENAC/eesd-modern-masonry-walls-db","event":"comment:6367598669"},"data":{"body":"Done in #41 another way: the design skill repo went private, so the design system is vendored in `frontend/vendor/epfl-design-system/` (commit 55fc0a8, no desktop font files) and fonts load from enac-it-fonts.epfl.ch. Ready for review."}}]}